For most of the last century, the deal was simple: someone made a thing, and everyone else watched it. Film, broadcast, the feed — a finished object, delivered to an audience that stayed on the far side of the glass.

We're building for a different deal. A world you can step inside, that changes because you're there.

## You're not watching. You're in it.

Infinite Spaces is where creatives of every kind build living, immersive worlds and invite people in. Not a video of a place — the place itself, running live, responding to the people moving through it. A concert where the crowd's motion becomes the lightshow. A venue that plays a different world every night. A room that remembers everyone who walked through.

World-building has never had a participatory layer the way film or gaming eventually did. That's the layer we're building.

## What lives here

This is the community site — the front porch. Expect:

- Notes from the people building worlds, and the tools underneath them
- Deep dives on the spatial tech that makes it feel instant — splats, real-time compositing, sub-125ms presence
- The occasional world you can step into right from the page

Speaking of which — here's one now. Scroll into it.

{% story slug="website-3dgs" /%}

That's a Gaussian-splat world running live in your browser. No plugin, no download. Just a place, and you in it.

## Come build with us

If you make things — paint, sound, movement, film, games, rooms — there's a place for what you make here, live, with people in it. This blog is where we'll show the work as it comes together.

Welcome in.
